WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.014
[MUSIC]

00:00:03.014 --> 00:00:09.750
The technology enablers are now there.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.939
And we're going to be
making that transition,

00:00:13.939 --> 00:00:18.509
just as we are into self-driving cars,
into things like digital

00:00:18.509 --> 00:00:22.599
currency transactions without
hardly even noticing it.

00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:26.812
For example, when you buy that
cup of coffee at Starbucks and

00:00:26.812 --> 00:00:28.882
you pay on your mobile phone.

00:00:28.882 --> 00:00:34.954
It could be that the application program
interface in your phone last week flipped

00:00:34.954 --> 00:00:40.771
from using your bank account to a payment
system based on digital currencies.

00:00:40.771 --> 00:00:45.292
And you might have gotten a brief
notice with five pages of fine print

00:00:45.292 --> 00:00:47.670
saying I agree at the end.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.660
And as long as you hit that button,

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.210
you just made that transition
without noticing it.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.297
I think it could be,
at the consumer level, as quick as that.

00:00:55.297 --> 00:01:00.193
That's not to say that it's simple.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:04.824
Hundreds of billions of dollars of
technology, software and hardware,

00:01:04.824 --> 00:01:08.343
need to be built around this,
particularly software.

00:01:08.343 --> 00:01:13.050
And a lot of legal work, and
a lot of regulatory work.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.110
And the central banks have to go along
with it before it'll be allowed.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.550
Because it's a concern,
it's part of the money supply.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.571
And central banks will be responsible for
monitoring that.

00:01:24.571 --> 00:01:29.480
And there are some countries that
are thinking about it, China, Sweden.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.103
Those are two countries that are currently
contemplating introducing digital

00:01:34.103 --> 00:01:38.935
currencies at the national level, through
the central banks of those countries.

00:01:38.935 --> 00:01:42.379
So change is coming, and

00:01:42.379 --> 00:01:46.971
I'm very interested in studying

00:01:46.971 --> 00:01:51.730
the implications of that change.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.428
[MUSIC]

